What this program takes from Walksnail OSD Tool
------------------------------------------------

The Kotlin sources translate, into another language, the OSD and font
logic in that project, mainly backend/src/osd and backend/src/font:

- The Walksnail .osd container. A 40-byte header, whose first four
  bytes are a flight-controller tag (BTFL, INAV, ARDU, KISS, or ULTR),
  followed by frames. Each frame is a 4-byte little-endian timestamp
  and a 53 by 20 grid of little-endian 16-bit glyph indexes. Indexes
  0x00 and 0x20 are empty. The duration is estimated from the first
  timestamp and the last timestamp.
- The PNG OSD font atlas. Tile sizes 18x27, 24x36, 36x54, 48x72, and
  72x108. One to four horizontal pages (standard, two-page,
  three-page, and four-color). 256 tiles per page. The same checks
  for an invalid width and an invalid height.
- Placement of each glyph on the video frame at grid position times
  tile size. The tile size follows the frame height (540, 720, 1080,
  1440, or 2160).

The desktop interface, the video reader, and the packaging are written
for this repository. They are a separate implementation from the Rust
egui application. This repository does not contain that project's
Rust sources.

What this repository does not take from Walksnail OSD Tool
----------------------------------------------------------

No font files, application icons, or FFmpeg binaries from
avsaase/walksnail-osd-tool are included here. An OSD font is a PNG
file that the user supplies.

That project's resources/fonts directory contains Inter-Regular.ttf,
AzeretMono-Regular.ttf, and SourceCodePro-Regular.ttf, used for its
own user interface, plus resources/fonts/OFL.txt. The copyright line
in that OFL file names the Inter Project Authors (2020) and the SIL
Open Font License 1.1. The same file does not name Azeret Mono or
Source Code Pro. Those files were not copied into this repository,
and this notice does not state a license for them.

